{
  "abstractions": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "ledger": [
        "abs-go-heap"
      ],
      "text": "Go heap: a list of backing arrays (byte values as Nat). A slice is (backing, offset, len, cap); append writes in place when len + k <= cap, else allocates a new backing array."
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "ledger": [
        "oracle-go-sizeclass-trunc512"
      ],
      "text": "Oracle (Go 1.24 runtime, runtime/slice.go nextslicecap + roundupsize for noscan byte slices): new capacity = smallest size class >= nextslicecap(newLen, oldCap). The class table (runtime/sizeclasses.go class_to_size) is in the state, truncated to classes <= 512 bytes: larger allocations are out of scope (the model then uses the exact requested capacity, which is wrong for real Go). The search policy keeps every slice below 512 bytes."
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "ledger": [
        "abs-newbatchdata-cap0"
      ],
      "text": "NewBatchData's make([]byte, 0) slices have capacity 0 and no backing array (backing index 0 is never written while cap = 0)."
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "ledger": [
        "scope-batchdata-unmodelled"
      ],
      "text": "l1TxHashes, blockNum and l1TxNum are not modelled (no aliasing relevant to TxsPayloadV2)."
    }
  ],
